# Ubuntu's own Blender for the Spark, so the temple rebuilds, the showpiece's live runs and the
# Blender tools run on the node like everything else (operator: "move everything to
# Spark", the Mac downloads a model only to look at it). Blender publishes no build for ARM Linux,
# not even a daily one; Ubuntu 26.04 packages 5.0.1 for arm64. The Mac has 5.2.1: a model made here
# opens there, and the temple saved there reads here piece for piece (model-anatomy on v25:
# the same 8,170 pieces by role and the same size on both). Ubuntu's build has no CUDA or OptiX, so
# Cycles would be stuck on the processor; the tools render with EEVEE and Workbench, which draw
# through OpenGL and do use the chip (deploy/spark/bin/blender). The node allows no
# system packages, so it lives in this image and deploy/spark/bin/blender runs it.
# Base: Ubuntu 26.04's minimal root filesystem, imported by build-blender.sh (Docker Hub is blocked
# on the node and NGC has no 26.04 image). Build: deploy/spark/build-blender.sh.
ARG BASE_IMAGE=beyond-canvas/ubuntu-base:26.04.1
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}
ARG DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
# Straight from Ubuntu's own archive, which the node reaches (334 packages, 299 MB, about ten
# minutes); apt checks every package's signature. Beside Blender: NumPy, which the
# survey tools and the glTF export import, and Mesa's EGL and OpenGL, which a headless render needs
# to draw at all: without them every render stopped at "Couldn't open libEGL.so.1", then at
# "libGL.so.1 or libOpenGL.so.0". They also draw it on the processor wherever the chip is missing,
# at about a twentieth of the speed. With them Workbench and EEVEE both render, after three harmless
# EGL_BAD_MATCH lines. And ffmpeg, which the
# tools call from inside Blender to turn their frames into raise.mp4, flow.mp4 and the rest; a tool
# that finds none skips its video without an error.
RUN apt-get update \
    && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends blender python3-numpy ffmpeg \
        libegl1 libegl-mesa0 libgl1-mesa-dri libopengl0 libgl1 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
    && blender --version | head -1 && ffmpeg -hide_banner -encoders | grep -q libx264
